2026-09-02T14:05:00.000Z note (out-of-band: requirements/errata.md E-1 written by hand at the requirements gate, BEFORE the chore run rather than during it, because the hazard is one an implementer would otherwise meet as a red suite in an environment row nobody chose. It rules that AC-19 asserts over the declared `files` allow-list and the entry point and never over a file count, a byte size or the absence of build output. Nothing in merged.md is false and no criterion is narrowed; what is added is the environment its numbers were taken in. Measured at 51c56f5: packages/* carry no .npmignore and no package-level .gitignore, and npm reads ignore files in the package directory only and never the repository root, so gitignored dist/ and .turbo/ ship — @quorum/cli packs 40 here against 22 in a fresh clone, @quorum/core 167 against 101, @quorum/shared 52 against 28. §3's three figures are all the built-checkout column. This is the assertion Q-0096's E-1 retired one ticket ago for the identical reason, one layer out and in the same subsystem. Also recorded: the inherited "22 files" is not stale but environment-dependent and COINCIDENTALLY EQUAL — 19 tracked + 3 turbo logs then, 22 tracked + 4 logs + 14 dist = 40 now, so a fresh clone today packs 22 and a careful reader re-measuring in a clean checkout appears to confirm the superseded figure. The same ruling is repeated in ticket.md as GO-5 for a human reader, with a pointer saying the erratum is the binding copy: chore.yaml's implement step reads requirements/merged.md, requirements/errata.md and the review files, and never ticket.md, so a rule recorded only in the body would not reach the implementer. ticket.md was edited AFTER the run completed, not during it, because the engine snapshots the ticket at run start and finish() writes it back.)
