2026-09-02T15:11:00.000Z note (out-of-band: DIAGNOSED BY EXPERIMENT rather than by reading. With packages/cli/dist/quorum.js absent at install time, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` links no shim; re-running the identical command once the artifact exists creates it ("Already up to date", 182 ms). So pnpm links a bin shim during INSTALL and only where the target exists, and the fixture's own runBuild() cannot make a finished install link anything. Decision 078(b) deliberately gives `test` no ^build edge, so from a clean checkout the order is install → test and dist/ is GUARANTEED absent when install runs — which makes AC-18's shim mechanism structurally incompatible with the ruling this ticket sits under, not a slip. The implementer's worktree had built before installing, so its verdict was a property of that checkout's ordering rather than of the commit. requirements/errata.md E-2 rules it; the fixture links the shim itself via linkBins(), which adds no task-graph edge so no other verdict moves behind a build, and registers its write to node_modules/.bin in place rather than hiding it.)
2026-09-02T15:12:00.000Z note (out-of-band: FINISHED BY HAND on Q-0096's precedent, the run having aborted. The fix is one helper and two call sites, committed to harness/Q-0098/implement at ba3a5fd; harness/Q-0098/implement merged --no-ff into harness/Q-0098/integration at 6b8c976. Verified in the integrate worktree, which is the fresh-checkout environment row: workspace 7/7 tasks 0 cached, cli 159 passed where the aborted run had 157 passed + 2 failed, core 1285 + 2 skipped, shared 150. linkBins() was then shown LOAD-BEARING rather than incidental by deleting node_modules/.bin/quorum and re-running: the four AC-18 tests pass and the shim is recreated, so it self-heals the exact state that failed integrate. No review round saw this fix — it is the operator's, and the two majors review round 3 raised about Windows are unaddressed and registered below.)
2026-09-02T15:13:00.000Z note (out-of-band: REGISTERED AND NOT FIXED — the POSIX-only build. Review iteration 3's single major was that `chmod +x dist/quorum.js` is POSIX-only, so `pnpm turbo run build` fails on Windows before the mode tests reach their skips. Real, and advanced past deliberately: `rm -rf dist` is the same defect in the same line and the reviewer did not flag it, all three emitting packages carry it, and it was Q-0097 (b5d36d9) that introduced `rm -rf dist &&` — so a genuine fix is a cross-platform build helper across three build scripts, which is Q-0097's surface and a design change rather than a repair. The repository has never claimed Windows support: all seven CI jobs are ubuntu-latest, and harness.yaml's own commands.install and commands.test are POSIX shell chains. AC-16's skip clause anticipated a platform without POSIX MODES for the ASSERTION, which round 3 implemented correctly with ctx.skip; the BUILD has been POSIX-only since Q-0097 and remains so. Wants its own ticket if Windows is ever a goal, because it is a decision and not a repair.)
